  "output": "## Test coverage analysis — `src/lib/content-types.ts`, `src/lib/articles.ts`, `src/lib/legal.ts`, `src/content/**`\n\n**Current state:** no test runner is configured (`package.json` has no `test` script, no Jest/Vitest dependency) and there are zero test files under `src/`. Everything below is therefore 0%-covered. I'd recommend Vitest (works cleanly with Next 16 + ESM, no babel config needed):\n\n```ts\n// vitest.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\nimport path from \"path\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  test: { environment: \"node\", include: [\"src/**/*.test.ts\"] },\n  resolve: { alias: { \"@\": path.resolve(__dirname, \"src\") } },\n});\n```\n```json\n// package.json additions\n\"scripts\": { \"test\": \"vitest run\" },\n\"devDependencies\": { \"vitest\": \"^3\" }\n```\n\n---\n\n### 1. `src/lib/content-types.ts`\n\n#### `anchorId(text: string): string`\nUntested. Edge cases not covered:\n- Empty string\n- Punctuation-only text (`\"???\"` → `\"\"`)\n- Non-ASCII / currency symbols dropped silently (`\"₹2 crore\"` appears verbatim in `aifs-india-what-why-trend.ts`)\n- Em-dash / curly-quote headings (`AIFs and \"Accredited Investors\" — why it matters` — real heading in the codebase) collapsing whitespace correctly instead of jamming words together\n- 60-char truncation: two long headings sharing the same first 60 characters produce **the same id** (collision bug)\n- Truncation cutting mid-word (cosmetic, but should be pinned down as documented behavior)\n\n```ts\n// src/lib/content-types.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { anchorId } from \"@/lib/content-types\";\n\ndescribe(\"anchorId\", () => {\n  it(\"lowercases and hyphenates a simple heading\", () => {\n    expect(anchorId(\"What is an AIF?\")).toBe(\"what-is-an-aif\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns empty string for empty input\", () => {\n    expect(anchorId(\"\")).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"strips punctuation without leaving stray hyphens\", () => {\n    expect(anchorId('AIFs and \"Accredited Investors\" — why it matters'))\n      .toBe(\"aifs-and-accredited-investors-why-it-matters\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"drops non-word currency symbols instead of erroring\", () => {\n    expect(anchorId(\"₹2 crore threshold\")).toBe(\"2-crore-threshold\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"truncates to 60 chars\", () => {\n    const long = \"a\".repeat(100);\n    expect(anchorId(long).length).toBeLessThanOrEqual(60);\n  });\n\n  it(\"FLAGGED GAP: two headings sharing a 60-char prefix collide\", () => {\n    const a = \"x\".repeat(60) + \" first ending\";\n    const b = \"x\".repeat(60) + \" second ending\";\n    // documents current (undesirable) behavior — should probably be fixed\n    // by hashing/disambiguating rather than silently colliding\n    expect(anchorId(a)).toBe(anchorId(b));\n  });\n});\n```\n\n#### `buildToc(blocks: RichBlock[]): {id, text}[]`\nUntested. Gaps: empty array, no-h2 case, mixed block kinds, duplicate-heading-text producing duplicate ids (propagates the `anchorId` collision above into a broken TOC).\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"buildToc\", () => {\n  it(\"returns [] for empty blocks\", () => {\n    expect(buildToc([])).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns [] when there are no h2 blocks\", () => {\n    expect(buildToc([{ kind: \"p\", text: \"hi\" }])).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  it(\"extracts only h2 blocks, ignoring h3/p/ul\", () => {\n    const blocks: RichBlock[] = [\n      { kind: \"h2\", text: \"Intro\" },\n      { kind: \"h3\", text: \"Sub\" },\n      { kind: \"p\", text: \"body\" },\n      { kind: \"h2\", text: \"Next\" },\n    ];\n    expect(buildToc(blocks)).toEqual([\n      { id: \"intro\", text: \"Intro\" },\n      { id: \"next\", text: \"Next\" },\n    ]);\n  });\n\n  it(\"FLAGGED GAP: duplicate h2 text produces duplicate ids (broken anchors)\", () => {\n    const blocks: RichBlock[] = [\n      { kind: \"h2\", text: \"Overview\" },\n      { kind: \"h2\", text: \"Overview\" },\n    ];\n    const toc = buildToc(blocks);\n    expect(toc[0].id).toBe(toc[1].id); // documents the bug — real pages will scroll to the wrong section\n  });\n});\n```\n\n#### `readingMinutes(blocks: RichBlock[]): number`\nUntested. Gaps:\n- Empty blocks → must floor at `1`, not `0`\n- Empty-string paragraph counted as `1` word (`\"\".split(/\\s+/)` → `[\"\"]`, length 1) — a genuine off-by-one bug source\n- `table` block: `columns` (headers) are **excluded** from the word count, only `rows` counted — undocumented, worth pinning\n- Rounding boundary at exactly 100/300 words\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"readingMinutes\", () => {\n  it(\"returns minimum 1 for empty content\", () => {\n    expect(readingMinutes([])).toBe(1);\n  });\n\n  it(\"FLAGGED GAP: an empty-text paragraph still counts as 1 word\", () => {\n    expect(readingMinutes([{ kind: \"p\", text: \"\" }])).toBe(1); // documents split(/\\s+/) quirk\n  });\n\n  it(\"counts words across p, ul, and table rows but not table columns\", () => {\n    const blocks: RichBlock[] = [\n      { kind: \"table\", columns: [\"Header one\", \"Header two\"], rows: [[\"a b c\", \"d e f\"]] },\n    ];\n    // header words (\"Header one Header two\" = 4 words) are NOT counted — only \"a b c d e f\" (6 words)\n    expect(readingMinutes(blocks)).toBe(1); // 6/200 -> max(1, round(0.03)) = 1\n  });\n\n  it(\"rounds at the 200-words-per-minute boundary\", () => {\n    const words = Array(300).fill(\"word\").join(\" \");\n    expect(readingMinutes([{ kind: \"p\", text: words }])).toBe(2); // 300/200 = 1.5 -> round -> 2\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. `src/lib/articles.ts`\n\nUntested functions: `getArticle`, `getArticleBody`, and the derived `ARTICLES_SORTED`.\n\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { ARTICLES, ARTICLES_SORTED, getArticle, getArticleBody, CATEGORY_GLYPH } from \"@/lib/articles\";\n\ndescribe(\"getArticle\", () => {\n  it(\"returns the matching article for a known slug\", () => {\n    expect(getArticle(\"market-outlook-2025\")?.title).toBe(\"Market Outlook 2025: Key Trends to Watch\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns undefined for an unknown slug\", () => {\n    expect(getArticle(\"does-not-exist\")).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n\n  it(\"is case-sensitive (documents current behavior)\", () => {\n    expect(getArticle(\"MARKET-OUTLOOK-2025\")).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns undefined for empty string\", () => {\n    expect(getArticle(\"\")).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"getArticleBody\", () => {\n  it(\"returns the ported body for a known slug\", () => {\n    expect(getArticleBody(\"power-of-asset-allocation\").length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns [] for a slug with no registered body (defensive default)\", () => {\n    expect(getArticleBody(\"no-such-slug\")).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"ARTICLES_SORTED\", () => {\n  it(\"is sorted newest-first by iso date\", () => {\n    const isoDates = ARTICLES_SORTED.map((a) => a.iso);\n    const sorted = [...isoDates].sort().reverse();\n    expect(isoDates).toEqual(sorted);\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not mutate the original ARTICLES array order\", () => {\n    expect(ARTICLES_SORTED).not.toBe(ARTICLES);\n    expect(ARTICLES.map((a) => a.slug)).toEqual(\n      ARTICLES.map((a) => a.slug) // sanity: original order unchanged after ARTICLES_SORTED was computed\n    );\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"CATEGORY_GLYPH\", () => {\n  it(\"has a glyph for every category used by an article\", () => {\n    for (const article of ARTICLES) {\n      expect(CATEGORY_GLYPH[article.category]).toBeDefined();\n    }\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. `src/lib/legal.ts`\n\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { LEGAL_DOCS, getLegalDoc } from \"@/lib/legal\";\n\ndescribe(\"getLegalDoc\", () => {\n  it(\"returns the doc for a known id\", () => {\n    expect(getLegalDoc(\"privacy-policy\")?.title).toBe(\"Privacy Policy\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns undefined for an unknown id\", () => {\n    expect(getLegalDoc(\"nonexistent-doc\")).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"LEGAL_DOCS integrity\", () => {\n  it(\"every entry's .id matches its dictionary key (lookup-by-id consistency)\", () => {\n    for (const [key, doc] of Object.entries(LEGAL_DOCS)) {\n      expect(doc.id).toBe(key);\n    }\n  });\n\n  it(\"every entry has a unique route path\", () => {\n    const paths = Object.values(LEGAL_DOCS).map((d) => d.path);\n    expect(new Set(paths).size).toBe(paths.length);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Content data-integrity tests (biggest actual gap)\n\nThe `articles.ts` and `legal.ts` file comments themselves flag this content as \"ported verbatim ... must be revalidated\" — but nothing currently verifies structural consistency between the metadata registry and the content bodies. This is the highest-value suite to add:\n\n```ts\n// src/content/content-integrity.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { ARTICLES } from \"@/lib/articles\";\nimport { ARTICLE_BODIES } from \"@/content/articles\";\nimport { LEGAL_DOCS } from \"@/lib/legal\";\nimport { buildToc, anchorId, type RichBlock } from \"@/lib/content-types\";\n\ndescribe(\"article/body registry consistency\", () => {\n  it(\"every article slug has a corresponding body entry\", () => {\n    for (const article of ARTICLES) {\n      expect(ARTICLE_BODIES[article.slug], `missing body for ${article.slug}`).toBeDefined();\n    }\n  });\n\n  it(\"every ARTICLE_BODIES key corresponds to a real article (no orphan content)\", () => {\n    const slugs = new Set(ARTICLES.map((a) => a.slug));\n    for (const slug of Object.keys(ARTICLE_BODIES)) {\n      expect(slugs.has(slug), `orphan body: ${slug}`).toBe(true);\n    }\n  });\n\n  it(\"every article's iso field is a well-formed YYYY-MM-DD string\", () => {\n    for (const a of ARTICLES) {\n      expect(a.iso).toMatch(/^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$/);\n    }\n  });\n});\n\nfunction tableRowsMatchColumns(blocks: RichBlock[]) {\n  return blocks\n    .filter((b): b is Extract<RichBlock, { kind: \"table\" }> => b.kind === \"table\")\n    .every((t) => t.rows.every((row) => row.length === t.columns.length));\n}\n\nfunction h2IdsAreUnique(blocks: RichBlock[]) {\n  const ids = buildToc(blocks).map((t) => t.id);\n  return new Set(ids).size === ids.length;\n}\n\ndescribe(\"rich content structural integrity\", () => {\n  const allBodies = [\n    ...Object.entries(ARTICLE_BODIES),\n    ...Object.values(LEGAL_DOCS).map((d) => [d.id, d.blocks] as const),\n  ];\n\n  it.each(allBodies)(\"%s: table rows match column count\", (_key, blocks) => {\n    expect(tableRowsMatchColumns(blocks)).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it.each(allBodies)(\"%s: h2 headings produce unique anchor ids\", (_key, blocks) => {\n    expect(h2IdsAreUnique(blocks)).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it.each(allBodies)(\"%s: ul/ol blocks have at least one item\", (_key, blocks) => {\n    for (const b of blocks) {\n      if (b.kind === \"ul\" || b.kind === \"ol\") {\n        expect(b.items.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n      }\n    }\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Missing error-handling coverage\n\nNone of these functions throw today — they all degrade to `undefined`/`[]` on bad input, which is good defensive design, but that behavior itself is unverified:\n- `getArticle`/`getLegalDoc`/`getArticleBody` never tested against `undefined`-shaped or unexpected slugs (only the \"happy path\" is implicit from usage in pages).\n- No test currently pins that these functions **don't throw** when given garbage input — worth a quick fuzz-style assertion (`expect(() => getArticle(garbage)).not.toThrow()`), since if a route ever passes `params.slug` unvalidated from a dynamic segment, a throw would crash the page instead of rendering a 404.\n\n### 6. Integration test gaps\n\n`src/app/insights/` (article detail pages) and `src/app/{privacy-policy,terms-and-condition,global-investing}/` presumably wire `getArticle` + `getArticleBody` + `buildToc` + `readingMinutes` / `getLegalDoc` together, but the context provided doesn't show those route files. Worth adding (once those files are reviewed):\n- A rendering test asserting an unknown `/insights/[slug]` renders `notFound()` rather than throwing.\n- A rendering test asserting every TOC link (`#anchor-id`) generated by `buildToc` matches an `id` actually present on a heading in the rendered DOM — this is where the `anchorId` collision bug above would manifest as a real broken link.\n- A route-existence check that every `LEGAL_DOCS[...].path` has a matching page file under `src/app`.\n\nWant me to scaffold these as actual files (`vitest.config.ts` + the test files above) and wire up the `test` script, or leave this as the analysis for now?\n",
