        "title": "4. Content data-integrity tests (biggest actual gap)",
        "content": "\nThe `articles.ts` and `legal.ts` file comments themselves flag this content as \"ported verbatim ... must be revalidated\" — but nothing currently verifies structural consistency between the metadata registry and the content bodies. This is the highest-value suite to add:\n\n```ts\n// src/content/content-integrity.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { ARTICLES } from \"@/lib/articles\";\nimport { ARTICLE_BODIES } from \"@/content/articles\";\nimport { LEGAL_DOCS } from \"@/lib/legal\";\nimport { buildToc, anchorId, type RichBlock } from \"@/lib/content-types\";\n\ndescribe(\"article/body registry consistency\", () => {\n  it(\"every article slug has a corresponding body entry\", () => {\n    for (const article of ARTICLES) {\n      expect(ARTICLE_BODIES[article.slug], `missing body for ${article.slug}`).toBeDefined();\n    }\n  });\n\n  it(\"every ARTICLE_BODIES key corresponds to a real article (no orphan content)\", () => {\n    const slugs = new Set(ARTICLES.map((a) => a.slug));\n    for (const slug of Object.keys(ARTICLE_BODIES)) {\n      expect(slugs.has(slug), `orphan body: ${slug}`).toBe(true);\n    }\n  });\n\n  it(\"every article's iso field is a well-formed YYYY-MM-DD string\", () => {\n    for (const a of ARTICLES) {\n      expect(a.iso).toMatch(/^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$/);\n    }\n  });\n});\n\nfunction tableRowsMatchColumns(blocks: RichBlock[]) {\n  return blocks\n    .filter((b): b is Extract<RichBlock, { kind: \"table\" }> => b.kind === \"table\")\n    .every((t) => t.rows.every((row) => row.length === t.columns.length));\n}\n\nfunction h2IdsAreUnique(blocks: RichBlock[]) {\n  const ids = buildToc(blocks).map((t) => t.id);\n  return new Set(ids).size === ids.length;\n}\n\ndescribe(\"rich content structural integrity\", () => {\n  const allBodies = [\n    ...Object.entries(ARTICLE_BODIES),\n    ...Object.values(LEGAL_DOCS).map((d) => [d.id, d.blocks] as const),\n  ];\n\n  it.each(allBodies)(\"%s: table rows match column count\", (_key, blocks) => {\n    expect(tableRowsMatchColumns(blocks)).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it.each(allBodies)(\"%s: h2 headings produce unique anchor ids\", (_key, blocks) => {\n    expect(h2IdsAreUnique(blocks)).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it.each(allBodies)(\"%s: ul/ol blocks have at least one item\", (_key, blocks) => {\n    for (const b of blocks) {\n      if (b.kind === \"ul\" || b.kind === \"ol\") {\n        expect(b.items.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n      }\n    }\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "5. Missing error-handling coverage",
        "content": "\nNone of these functions throw today — they all degrade to `undefined`/`[]` on bad input, which is good defensive design, but that behavior itself is unverified:\n- `getArticle`/`getLegalDoc`/`getArticleBody` never tested against `undefined`-shaped or unexpected slugs (only the \"happy path\" is implicit from usage in pages).\n- No test currently pins that these functions **don't throw** when given garbage input — worth a quick fuzz-style assertion (`expect(() => getArticle(garbage)).not.toThrow()`), since if a route ever passes `params.slug` unvalidated from a dynamic segment, a throw would crash the page instead of rendering a 404.\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "6. Integration test gaps",
        "content": "`src/app/insights/` (article detail pages) and `src/app/{privacy-policy,terms-and-condition,global-investing}/` presumably wire `getArticle` + `getArticleBody` + `buildToc` + `readingMinutes` / `getLegalDoc` together, but the context provided doesn't show those route files. Worth adding (once those files are reviewed):\n- A rendering test asserting an unknown `/insights/[slug]` renders `notFound()` rather than throwing.\n- A rendering test asserting every TOC link (`#anchor-id`) generated by `buildToc` matches an `id` actually present on a heading in the rendered DOM — this is where the `anchorId` collision bug above would manifest as a real broken link.\n- A route-existence check that every `LEGAL_DOCS[...].path` has a matching page file under `src/app`.\n\nWant me to scaffold these as actual files (`vitest.config.ts` + the test files above) and wire up the `test` script, or leave this as the analysis for now?",
        "level": 3
      }
    ],
